    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0544" n="502" xml:id="pg502"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 218</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">840B.062/4–1851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Legation in Iceland
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d218-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-20T20:00:00-05:00">April 20, 1951—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. In order reply Legtel 210 Apr 18<anchor n="2" xml:id="d218-f2"/> we need
                    your and FonMin further views re: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Possibility that arrival of troops before May 18 might precipitate
                            strike earlier than scheduled.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Feeling of Govt, labor, and public which wld indicate any possibility
                            avoiding strike and if not, its seriousness, possible duration,
                            difficulties in way of settlement.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Possibility signing agreement as soon possible, and then keeping it
                            secret for period long enough permit later entry of troops, say June.
                            Wld this jeopardize Agreement if Govt thinks Althing action
                            necessary?</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Destroyers <hi rendition="#italic">Brownson</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Meredith</hi> scheduled visit Reykjavik Apr 28–May 1. If troops not
                    available wld lay-over or somewhat later arrival these ships be useful and
                    permit announcement agreement? Both above queries exploratory only as no firm
                    assurance can yet be given that destroyers cld delay their schedule, and no
                    decision yet made that this course advisable.</p>
                <p>Assume FonMin desires coincident arrival troops and announcement agreement order
                    to avoid public disturbances. Has he any other reasons? Has he considered
                    propaganda value to Soviet of arrival coincident with announcement, giving
                    appearance whole procedure rigged by two Govts fearing Ice public reaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
